flowchart TD
  accTitle: Centered mobile navigation menu behavior
  accDescr {
    When a reader opens the mobile navigation menu, a dimmed backdrop appears and the menu panel is centered in the viewport. Its labels are centered independently of their arrows, and reduced-motion preferences disable the new animations.
  }
  toggle["Reader opens mobile navigation"] --> backdrop["Fixed dimmed and blurred backdrop"]
  toggle --> panel["Panel fixed at viewport center"]
  panel --> layout["Centered label; trailing arrow in separate column"]
  panel --> bounds["Width and height constrained; vertical scrolling remains available"]
  motion{"Reduced-motion preference?"}
  motion -- No --> animation["Backdrop fades; panel fades/scales; options stagger in"]
  motion -- Yes --> disabled["Backdrop, panel, and option animations disabled"]
  panel -. Escape or outside click .-> closed["Existing close behavior; Escape returns focus to toggle"]
